# Force LF checkout for the app's data/text assets, regardless of a
# contributor's global core.autocrlf setting. Several of these files are
# split into fields by OperationBand/RigNameList parsers that only split
# lines on "\n" -- a CRLF checkout (the default on Windows with
# core.autocrlf=true and no override) leaves a trailing "\r" on each line's
# last field. For bands.txt specifically, that silently broke every
# waveLength comparison (isBandExcluded, mostUsedBands, getModeBandFreq, ...)
# on every Windows-built APK, with no error anywhere -- the Band & Mode sheet
# just came up empty. Scoped to the whole assets directory's .txt files
# rather than just the ones confirmed affected: the failure mode is silent,
# so there's little reason to assume only the known files are exposed, and
# forcing LF costs nothing for the ones that are just display-only help text.
ft8af/app/src/main/assets/*.txt text eol=lf
